From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lkshrk <dev@harke.me>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:26:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] Report only runtimes that wrote an MCP server as
 configured

The native ownership check sends every self-defined and registry server
through every target runtime. On runtimes without a native comparison the
server already exists, so the safe installer skips it, yet the summary
listed that runtime as configured and printed an "already configured,
skipping" warning on every install. The summary now names only runtimes
that wrote the server, and a skip caused by the forced re-check is
reported at verbose level only.
